      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S009",
      "patient_response": "Well, Doc, I guess what brings me in is I just keep forgetting things I really shouldn’t. Important stuff, you know? Like my heart follow-up appointments. I’ll completely miss them, or I'll forget to call the clinic back when they leave a message. Which reminds me, the receptionist at that clinic, she has the exact same voice as my sister-in-law. It’s uncanny. Every time she calls, I think it’s Martha calling to complain about her gutters again. I told Martha she needs to just bite the bullet and get those leaf guards installed, but she won't listen. \n\nAnyway, where was I? Oh, right, forgetting things. It’s not just the doctors. I do a lot of tinkering and repair jobs around the neighborhood since I retired, just to keep busy, you know? And I’ll show up to fix a cabinet or a pipe, and I completely forgot to bring the right tools. I’ll have a whole toolbox with me and not a single wrench I actually need for the job. It's just getting frustrating.",
